NOTICE

This project adapts engineering patterns (not source code) from Anthropic's
commerce-agents blueprint (https://github.com/anthropics/commerce-agents) and
the guide "The anatomy of effective commerce agents"
(https://claude.com/blog/the-anatomy-of-effective-commerce-agents).

Adapted patterns, and where they live in this repo:
  - Staged change + change ledger, guardrails at stage AND apply time
    -> approvals/ledger.py (decision-time double gate)
  - MerchantBackend typed tool interface, model reads results not raw HTTP
    -> tools/forecast_tool.py, tools/campaign_tool.py
  - MerchantAgentConfig (enable_* switches, guardrail limits, one frozen config)
    -> app/config.py (DecisionAgentConfig)
  - build_static_system / build_dynamic_context prompt split, cache breakpoint
    -> rag/llm_explainer.py
  - Grounding lexicon and claim gates
    -> rag/llm_explainer.py (lexicon_check), rag/explainer.py
  - Presentation tools as typed payload schemas enriched by the host
    -> presentation/cards.py
  - DataLimitation: a figure the upstream cannot supply is typed evidence
    -> tools/forecast_tool.py
  - scripts/check.py cross-module drift gates
    -> scripts/check.py
  - Declarative flow specs (SKILL.md style), drift-checked against the planner
    -> decision_engine/flows/

The decision core itself is deliberately NOT an LLM agent loop: this service
is a scheduled sweep + API decision system in which the deterministic engine
decides, the LLM only rephrases grounded explanations, and humans approve
material actions.

This project also builds on dunnhumby's "The Complete Journey" dataset; see
rag/sources/ and docs/rag_sources.md for dataset attribution and license notes.